00:23:37.630 --> 00:23:39.360
Back at Howard actually
worked in admissions,

00:23:39.360 --> 00:23:40.340
that's my work study.

00:23:40.340 --> 00:23:42.590
And I found out about a
lot of processes that,

00:23:42.590 --> 00:23:44.050
many people don't know about

00:23:44.050 --> 00:23:46.250
such as something called
an appeals process.

00:23:47.124 --> 00:23:49.210
I encourage everyone to call
their admissions department,

00:23:49.210 --> 00:23:52.870
and let's say you do receive
a no from a university,

00:23:52.870 --> 00:23:54.740
first and foremost and
there was only two letters.

00:23:54.740 --> 00:23:58.570
So I know it may stink in the time being,

00:23:58.570 --> 00:24:00.070
but again, it's only two letters,

00:24:00.070 --> 00:24:05.070
there's possibilities and
ways to get that acceptance,

00:24:05.840 --> 00:24:08.097
if you would call their
admissions department and just,

00:24:08.097 --> 00:24:10.300
"Hey, do you guys have
an appeals process?"

00:24:10.300 --> 00:24:11.570
And in that appeals process,

00:24:11.570 --> 00:24:14.060
you essentially go
before a group of people,

00:24:14.060 --> 00:24:16.230
and honestly plead your case,

00:24:16.230 --> 00:24:17.063
'cause that sounds weird,(chuckle),

00:24:17.063 --> 00:24:19.087
