00:24:19.087 --> 00:24:23.900
"Hey, I was testing low in
this subject because of this,

00:24:23.900 --> 00:24:28.900
my ACT score is low
because of this situation."

00:24:28.993 --> 00:24:30.797
Really just explaining to them.

00:24:30.797 --> 00:24:32.520
"Hey, I would love to
be at this university,

00:24:32.520 --> 00:24:35.232
I would be an asset to this university,

00:24:35.232 --> 00:24:36.390
I wanna be here."

00:24:36.390 --> 00:24:39.000
And a lot of times those
university will hear you out.

00:24:39.000 --> 00:24:41.130
And hopefully a lot of the times,

00:24:41.130 --> 00:24:43.800
those denials turns into acceptances,

00:24:43.800 --> 00:24:46.250
I just wanted to add
that in there,(chuckle).

00:24:46.250 --> 00:24:47.570
- Yeah, that's super helpful.

00:24:47.570 --> 00:24:50.210
You know, my takeaway hearing
y'all and this gels with

00:24:50.210 --> 00:24:52.640
what I think too is, as all of y'all said,

00:24:52.640 --> 00:24:53.820
grades are valuable,

00:24:53.820 --> 00:24:54.980
they're valuable indicator,

00:24:54.980 --> 00:24:57.030
they can correlate with your work ethic,

00:24:57.030 --> 00:24:59.710
and your critical thinking
skills and all of that.

00:24:59.710 --> 00:25:02.780
And if you get good grades and
if you get good test scores,

00:25:02.780 --> 00:25:04.650
it will open up doors for you,

00:25:04.650 --> 00:25:07.170
people will give you the
benefit of the doubt.

00:25:07.170 --> 00:25:11.060
But with that said, if
you don't get them one,

00:25:11.060 --> 00:25:13.690
I've seen the trend matters
more than the absolute.

00:25:13.690 --> 00:25:14.910
So if you have some weaker grades,

00:25:14.910 --> 00:25:17.260
but they improve over
time, that's a great thing.

00:25:17.260 --> 00:25:19.110
In fact, that some ways shows,

00:25:19.110 --> 00:25:21.040
something even more special
about your character,

00:25:21.040 --> 00:25:23.710
that you can overcome
some of that adversity,

00:25:23.710 --> 00:25:25.487
and that even if your
grades aren't where you want

00:25:25.487 --> 00:25:26.880
are your standardized test scores,

00:25:26.880 --> 00:25:27.713
as you just mentioned,

00:25:27.713 --> 00:25:29.480
Madison and Delisha
mentioned this a lot as well,

00:25:29.480 --> 00:25:32.580
that there's other ways to
show what you're capable of.

00:25:32.580 --> 00:25:35.140
And frankly, the further
you get from college,

00:25:35.140 --> 00:25:38.210
the further that people run
an index on other things,

00:25:38.210 --> 00:25:39.120
other than those grades.

00:25:39.120 --> 00:25:40.750
And I'd say the other way around,

00:25:40.750 --> 00:25:43.330
we also all know students
who have straight A's,

00:25:43.330 --> 00:25:46.130
but if they didn't or perfect
standardized test scores,

00:25:46.130 --> 00:25:47.520
but if they didn't do the things,

00:25:47.520 --> 00:25:48.610
that all of y'all have done,

00:25:48.610 --> 00:25:51.560
when you're asked a lot of questions,

00:25:51.560 --> 00:25:53.460
but, always be pushing yourself.

00:25:53.460 --> 00:25:54.310
As Delisha mentioned,

00:25:54.310 --> 00:25:56.250
am I taking a bet on myself,

00:25:56.250 --> 00:25:57.810
and my stepping out of my comfort zone?

00:25:57.810 --> 00:25:59.370
Am I willing to take some risks?

00:25:59.370 --> 00:26:03.600
Am I willing to go talk to
people and risk getting rejected?

00:26:03.600 --> 00:26:06.160
A lot of folks, I've seen a
lot of very capable people,

00:26:06.160 --> 00:26:09.440
afraid to apply for an
opportunity for fear of rejection.

00:26:09.440 --> 00:26:11.640
And the only way to guarantee
